   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.1. Increased capacity of Member States to formulate and implement national employment policies in response to the COVID-19 crisis</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In March 2022, the Revolutionary Government of Zanzibar constituted a triparte task force led by the Ministry of State President&apos;s Office Labour, Economic and Investment to develop a Zanzibar Youth Employment Action Plan (2023 &#x2013; 2028) that will provide programmes and intervention areas to enhance youth employability and promote youth entrepreneurship. After tripartipte consultations, in June 2023 the Ministry of Labour finalized the Action Plan, which will begin parliament approval processes in October 2023. The Action plan has integrated gender, environmental concerns and the COVID-19 crisis and will highlight key challenges faced by young women and men to enter and remain in the labour market and incorporates new initiatives for creation of productive and decent work. With the support from one fund; TZA/17/03/OUF, UNDAP II - Economic Growth and Employment, the ILO supported the Revolutionary Government of Zanzibar and constituents with technical guidance on review processes in line with the ILO&#x2019;s Guidelines for implementation of employment policies: From policy to results, and the ILO decade for youth (2020-30) &#x2013;  to review the Zanzibar Youth Employment Action Plan (ZYEAP) of 2013 with the view of assessing progress made towards the outputs/performance indicators and to identify challenges encountered in its implementation that would inform the development of ZYEAP III (2023-2025).
From January through November 2022, ILO facilitated several technical committee meetings on the draft, in consultation with Development Partners, UN system and Civil Society Organizations (CSO) in Zanzibar. ILO technical assistance was also provided in reviewing these drafts and presentation to senior ministry and government management.  ILO was also involved from the drafting stage of the Terms of Reference (ToRs) for the consultant and was part of the tripartite technical committee task force that constituted seven tripartite members led by the Ministry of State President&apos;s Office Labour, Economic and Investment.. 

ILO facilitated the stakeholder consultation workshop on the draft on 9 November 2022, where 57 stakeholders (57 stakeholders have contributed to the development of the ZYEAP III (Government institutions: 38, Private sector:9, LGAs:7, Youth representatives:3) and other stakeholders were also in attendance. 
ILO has technically and financially supported the Revolutionary Government of Zanzibar to align the new Action Plan with the SDGs and national developoement frameworks as well as to ensure  gender mainastreaming. The ZYEAP III Action Plan was finalized in July 2022 and is awaiting Government approval processes.</narrative>
   </description>
